WEBVTT

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:11.820
Stop calling me by my first name and acting so personal.

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:17.490
Even if I look like your Hina, I'm not her.

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:21.000
Now there's not a single clue left.

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:24.000
I guess I can't go back.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:26.840
I'll have to live here forever.

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:36.910
Spread your wings

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:41.540
See the light of hope in the sky you have yet to witness

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:44.840
And don't ever give in to the weight of sorrow

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:50.220
Echo unto eternity, "Unisonia"

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:59.480
That world you see before your eyes

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:05.060
I wonder what colors it is made of

00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:09.530
The pain of loss isn't something

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:12.490
You want to get used to, and yet

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:17.450
Even on a night like this, the stars glisten

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:24.420
Like a tarnished coin spilling from the palm of your hand

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:26.250
Can't go back

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:27.670
Want to go home

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:31.010
The two of them back-to-back

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:33.050
Break through

00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:37.810
Turning unfading emotions into a lasting bond

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:41.140
Like painting over a colorless world

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:43.850
Let this sympathy reach

00:01:45.190 --> 00:01:50.110
Let's build the future that we envision

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:53.320
You'll see, we'll even change fate

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:58.120
Transcending time, "Unisonia"

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:07.730
It's been a long time, Vice-Admiral Richardson.

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:11.480
You're running awfully late, I see.

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:13.370
My apologies.

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:16.610
We happened to stumble across Zogilia's Imperial Army en route.

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:19.280
I heard we almost lost a new-type mecha.

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:23.120
Well, even if we did lose it, it would've had no impact on the status of the war.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:27.500
I've also confirmed that you will be participating in the next mission.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:30.330
Make sure you don't slow us down.

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:33.420
Good morning, everybody!

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:37.380
Pro-Professor!

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:38.590
Hold it!

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:42.090
This is a top secret communication line! How in the world did you join?!

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:43.100
Hmm...

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:44.470
You're a nuisance.

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:45.400
Wha—?

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:48.480
Well then, let's try this again.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:51.600
How are you doing, crew members of the Cygnus?

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:55.520
I see you haven't changed much, Doctor Fermi.

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:58.860
Captain. There's a ship approaching us from the front.

00:02:59.270 --> 00:03:02.360
It's the Coupling System Test Ship, the Crane.

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:15.500
Welcome to the Cygnus.

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:18.750
Oh, thank you, beautiful young lady.

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:21.180
I'm glad to see you're well, Professor.

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:22.550
Thank you.

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:27.260
You seem to have more wrinkles than before.

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:30.730
You've got to be kidding, Professor.

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:33.230
Now then, without further ado...

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:35.980
A demonstration of the Coupling system?

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:37.070
That's right.

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:39.250
Doctor Fermi would like to see it.

00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:40.670
Nice to meet you.

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:43.700
He came all the way from Hawaii just to see it.

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:44.990
From Hawaii?

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:49.410
Yup. Hawaii, where we'll be arriving soon.

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:51.460
Obviously he can't wait.

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:53.210
But, Luxon is now...

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:58.300
Luckily the cockpit wasn't damaged.
It can still be used for Coupling.

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:05.550
That old man is the developer of the Coupling System?

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:09.460
Not exactly. He's the leader of
the Coupling development team.

00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:10.680
What do you mean?

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:15.150
As far as I know, Doctor Fermi was the
first to propose the Coupling theory...

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:19.900
His research lab led the development of the system, but...

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:26.780
The cockpit Elvira-san developed was the
final piece needed for practical application.

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:32.750
In other words, the disciple took all the credit from the airhead teacher, right?

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:34.710
D-Doctor...

00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:38.000
Well, I've no problem being the airhead teacher.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:38.710
Huh?

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:44.470
You know, I started the underlying research of Coupling with Elvira-kun's grandfather.

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:48.510
So I've known her since she was still in diapers.

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:50.180
Oh, I see.

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:53.930
We were worried because it
took so long for her potty training.

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:55.390
Professor!

00:04:56.410 --> 00:04:58.770
But anyway, that little girl

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:01.730
is now a better researcher than me.

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:04.490
How could I not be happy about this?

00:05:05.050 --> 00:05:07.030
That's a nice story you have.

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:11.410
Enough with the chitchat. Let's begin the test. Ensign Watase!

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:13.250
Connect with Dio.

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:14.660
Accept.

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:23.140
Emphater waveform levels are stable.

00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:27.800
Isn't it beautiful to see such a high level of enharmonic control completion?

00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:30.350
How long does the Coupling connection last?

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:33.020
The practical limit is 300 seconds.

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:34.280
Perfect!

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:45.150
Ten seconds to Decoupling.

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:48.910
5, 4, 3,

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:50.870
2, 1...

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:52.610
Decoupling.

00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:59.960
The system and pilots show no abnormalities.

00:06:00.490 --> 00:06:02.960
Great work, Aoba-kun, Dio.

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:04.050
Thanks.

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:16.230
What?

00:06:16.230 --> 00:06:19.400
You may be able to fool a machine,
but you can't fool me.

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:21.440
What do you mean "fool you"?

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:25.500
You met her on that island,
didn't you? That girl named Hina.

00:06:26.140 --> 00:06:27.070
Nope.

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:28.860
That's such a barefaced lie.

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:32.530
It's the truth. That's not the Hina I knew.

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:33.330
What?

00:06:34.230 --> 00:06:38.960
Here, in this world 70 years into the future, there's no Hina.

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:44.750
The Yumihara Hina who saved me and
sent me into the future no longer exists.

00:06:45.610 --> 00:06:46.800
I see.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:48.730
So that's why you've been depressed.

00:06:48.730 --> 00:06:50.090
I'm not depressed.

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:51.970
You're surprisingly sensitive, aren't you?

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:53.720
I already told you I'm not depressed!

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:58.670
To begin with, that whole "enemy pilot
knows how to return to the past" thing...

00:06:58.670 --> 00:07:00.500
Where did you get that story from?

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:04.020
Even a kid could come up with something better than that.

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:09.030
I didn't make it up! It seemed to me
to be the only possible explanation.

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:10.450
Fine, I won't bring it up again.

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:18.190
What the hell?!

00:07:18.190 --> 00:07:19.250
Are you awake now?

00:07:19.690 --> 00:07:21.960
How long are you gonna sulk?

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:24.000
Luxon's almost fully repaired.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:25.840
Even someone like you, we're better off having you than—

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:29.470
<i>You</i> are the one who's sulking!

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:35.640
A guy who's been worrying about his little sister

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:38.060
has no right to lecture me!

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:39.350
You...

00:07:41.910 --> 00:07:43.230
Leave Fiona out of this!

00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:46.770
You damn siscon!

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:48.860
Shut up, you stubborn ass!

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:52.950
Damn you!

00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:54.240
Whoa!

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:56.330
You bastard!

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:57.780
What are you guys doing?!

00:07:57.780 --> 00:07:59.160
Stop it, Dio!

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:01.660
Let me go! I said let me go!

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:03.420
I'm just trying to wake this idiot up!

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:05.130
Shut up!

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:09.630
Man, you guys caused us a lot of trouble.

00:08:09.630 --> 00:08:12.010
Both of you went a little overboard.

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:15.550
Captain said to cool your heads down here for a while.

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:16.510
See ya'.

00:08:16.510 --> 00:08:18.470
Made me work up a sweat for nothing.

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:19.770
Geez...

00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:29.230
Isn't it great being young?

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:31.150
Oh?

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:33.030
Where's Doctor Fermi?

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:33.950
Eh?

00:08:34.600 --> 00:08:36.700
Now that you mention it...

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:40.120
Ah, here you are.

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:42.660
You claim to have come from the past?

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:45.290
70 years ago, was it?

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:47.290
You won't believe me anyway.

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:53.130
How much do you know about the Coupling System?

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:54.130
Eh?

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:55.340
To put it simply,

00:08:55.340 --> 00:09:03.770
it connects the brains of two pilots in parallel
and boosts the original source of power.

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:05.270
I see.

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:10.940
The system functions to transmit
the thoughts of both pilots instantly.

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:14.360
If there were a time lag,
it would be an obstacle during battle.

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:16.320
It transmits thoughts instantly?

00:09:16.680 --> 00:09:19.740
It's a waste of time explaining details to that idiot.

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:21.460
What did you say?

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:23.220
Oh yeah.

00:09:23.220 --> 00:09:28.130
Right now, you guys are only separated by a thin wall so the two of you can communicate like so.

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:30.670
However, that's not the case in a battle.

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:34.340
The larger the distance, the longer the delay.

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:40.390
Even a seven-second delay is enough to prevent Coupling.

00:09:40.390 --> 00:09:43.970
So then, how did we manage to perform a Coupling?

00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:47.190
Time leap.

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:47.980
What?

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:52.630
If there's a seven-second delay while transmitting thoughts,

00:09:52.630 --> 00:09:56.780
then we can send them seven seconds
into the furture to resolve the problem.

00:09:56.780 --> 00:09:59.160
Is that even possible?

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:01.870
Yes, at an elemental particle level.

00:10:02.180 --> 00:10:04.370
Elemental particle level?

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:06.120
What's so funny?

00:10:06.120 --> 00:10:10.540
It means the professor doesn't believe your story after all.

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:11.500
What the hell?

00:10:12.940 --> 00:10:14.960
You two look like you get along well.

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:17.050
Very well.

00:10:24.610 --> 00:10:28.100
You're implementing the Coupling system on the new plane?

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:30.980
You haven't heard? We're rolling it out soon.

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:32.690
Although there's only going to be two of them.

00:10:33.050 --> 00:10:36.900
The superiors have softened up a bit.

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:40.280
So does that mean the mass production of Coupling mechas won't be far off?

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:43.080
Unfortunately, we're not at that stage yet.

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:46.300
The Alliance doesn't think the
Coupling System is very important.

00:10:46.300 --> 00:10:49.210
Yet our enemies are desperate to get their hands on it...

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:51.750
Because that guy is in Zogilia.

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:52.580
That guy?

00:10:52.930 --> 00:10:54.250
A researcher from the professor's lab,

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:58.760
like me, defected to Zogilia.

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:01.220
He was a smart one too.

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:06.140
He must've understood the
importance of Elvira-kun's cockpit.

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:07.970
Who is this guy?

00:11:08.330 --> 00:11:11.690
Hahn, Wilhelm Hahn.

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:14.900
I think it's an interesting plan.

00:11:15.310 --> 00:11:19.490
Alright. I'll talk to the Administration Bureau about it.

00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:22.200
Thank you very much, Doctor Hahn.

00:11:22.590 --> 00:11:25.830
Do your best, Secret Services Agent Margaret.

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:29.370
Because this will be your last chance.

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:32.500
I'll pray for your success.

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:34.210
Glory to Zogilia!

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:42.220
That's the outline of this plan.

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:44.010
Any questions?

00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:44.680
Lieutenant Colonel.

00:11:45.410 --> 00:11:48.470
Who is this Dr. Hahn?

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:52.590
To have such influence on the Administration Bureau even though he's just a scientist.

00:11:52.590 --> 00:11:53.850
He must be someone important.

00:11:53.850 --> 00:11:56.790
You don't need to worry about that.

00:11:59.900 --> 00:12:03.410
I'll be in charge for today.

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:07.530
Is that alright, Lieutenant Colonel?

00:12:07.530 --> 00:12:10.000
Let her be.

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:18.960
It's me, Watase Aoba!

00:12:19.170 --> 00:12:20.710
I'll pull you out.

00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:23.220
I just wanted you to have it.

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:25.300
Watase Aoba.

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:26.270
Hina?

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:28.810
Bizon!

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:31.600
What happened? You look so serious.

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:35.600
Hina, how did you transmit that signal?

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:43.240
We arrived shortly after receiving it.

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:47.740
However, Fortuna's cockpit had already sunk into the ocean.

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:51.120
From the Alliance new-type.

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:52.790
What?! Then you...

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:55.250
No! I found it in the forest.

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:57.880
I was going to take it but the enemy came back.

00:12:57.880 --> 00:13:02.340
I only sent out an SOS signal because I was unarmed.

00:13:02.710 --> 00:13:06.720
But the only Valiancer there was Fortuna.

00:13:07.240 --> 00:13:09.760
It left just before you arrived.

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:12.770
I was hiding, so I couldn't see well.

00:13:14.360 --> 00:13:16.730
You don't believe me, right?

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:18.630
It's too good to be true.

00:13:20.270 --> 00:13:22.370
Have you told the Lieutenant Colonel?

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:24.150
Not yet.

00:13:24.150 --> 00:13:25.950
Tell that to the Lieutenant Colonel.

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:29.520
If the Secret Services Agent finds out first, it could spell trouble.

00:13:30.190 --> 00:13:31.200
You're right.

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:34.540
Tell me right away next time.

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:37.650
I'll believe you, no matter what.

00:13:38.340 --> 00:13:39.500
I understand.

00:13:40.680 --> 00:13:44.090
Bizon, there's not much time.
Board your mecha immediately.

00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:45.590
Yes, sir.

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:02.820
Enemy Valiancers approaching.

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:03.900
Contact in 10 minutes.

00:14:04.370 --> 00:14:06.440
Everyone, prepare for battle!

00:14:08.810 --> 00:14:10.490
Come on out. It's time for battle.

00:14:20.070 --> 00:14:23.210
Is it alright to release them in that condition?

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:23.920
Eh?

00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:26.510
Aren't they always that way?

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:29.050
I guess that's true, but...

00:14:29.990 --> 00:14:31.050
They're here!

00:14:31.050 --> 00:14:32.850
Spread out and be ready to fight!

00:14:32.850 --> 00:14:33.810
Roger!

00:14:34.530 --> 00:14:37.930
Don't think of anything else,
just focus on the battle.

00:14:37.930 --> 00:14:39.820
I know that!

00:14:39.820 --> 00:14:43.110
Aoba-san, Dio. Please start Coupling.

00:14:43.110 --> 00:14:44.900
Roger.

00:14:45.320 --> 00:14:46.440
Connect with Dio.

00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:47.780
Accept.

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:55.490
A number of photothermal formations are approaching.

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:57.870
They're Zogilian cruise missiles!

00:14:57.870 --> 00:14:59.290
Nectar Curtain, activate!

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:04.680
Damage report?

00:15:04.680 --> 00:15:06.920
Minimal damage. No problems reported.

00:15:07.240 --> 00:15:08.340
Second volley approaching!

00:15:08.690 --> 00:15:11.590
The Cygnus' Nectar Curtain won't be recharged in time.

00:15:11.590 --> 00:15:14.180
All units, shoot down as many missiles as possible!

00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:15.060
Roger!

00:15:21.020 --> 00:15:22.310
Wha—?

00:15:22.310 --> 00:15:24.610
There's no time to hesitate!

00:15:27.970 --> 00:15:28.820
I can be...

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:33.530
Wait and see, Hina. I'll finish this guy!

00:15:35.500 --> 00:15:36.370
Aoba.

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:39.620
Lieutenant Colonel. Cover me!

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:40.410
Understood.

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:43.420
That guy again.

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:45.880
You're stubborn.

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:54.590
Damn it.

00:15:56.100 --> 00:15:57.010
They got through?!

00:15:59.890 --> 00:16:01.020
The Crane has been hit.

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:04.400
Lieutenant Conrad, destroy all the
missiles heading towards the Crane.

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:06.230
Don't let any missiles through!

00:16:06.230 --> 00:16:08.480
There's no need for that.

00:16:08.850 --> 00:16:09.900
Professor!

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:13.570
I'm okay. The Crane won't get shot down that easily.

00:16:14.420 --> 00:16:15.660
But...!

00:16:16.190 --> 00:16:20.660
Elvira-kun, I've taught you everything your grandfather taught me.

00:16:21.170 --> 00:16:23.210
It's time to move on.

00:16:24.280 --> 00:16:26.960
I'll leave the future in your hands.

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:30.880
Can we really shoot down this many?

00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:33.470
No time for whining! Just do what you have to do!

00:16:37.550 --> 00:16:38.970
Amazing...

00:16:38.970 --> 00:16:41.520
As expected of Aoba-san and Dio.

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:45.270
Now we just have to wait for the
enemy to use up all their missiles.

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:48.520
It would be great if they use them all up.

00:16:51.230 --> 00:16:52.780
Another volley of missiles are heading this way!

00:16:53.110 --> 00:16:54.990
How many did they prepare?!

00:16:55.340 --> 00:16:56.110
Could it be...?

00:16:56.110 --> 00:16:59.080
They're waiting for the Coupling's time limit.

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:01.450
Based on Doctor Hahn's predictions,

00:17:01.450 --> 00:17:05.000
their Coupling is limited to 300 seconds.

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:07.290
Which means they only have 90 seconds remaining.

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:12.550
After Decoupling, we won't be
able to handle this many missiles.

00:17:12.870 --> 00:17:16.090
Don't slack off! There are still some missiles coming!

00:17:16.090 --> 00:17:17.590
But the Coupling...

00:17:18.020 --> 00:17:20.010
Don't give up, Watase Aoba!

00:17:20.890 --> 00:17:24.980
Didn't you decide to stay on the Cygnus and fight?

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:27.900
You're an idiot. A bona fide idiot.

00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:32.940
Aren't you the kind of guy who will
do whatever it takes, no matter what?

00:17:33.530 --> 00:17:35.900
Right now, the Cygnus is in need of power.

00:17:36.220 --> 00:17:40.160
And you have that power to help them.

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:43.160
Fight! For the people who need your help!

00:17:44.410 --> 00:17:46.540
Hurry up, you crybaby!

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:51.000
Damn it!

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:51.540
It got through!

00:17:54.920 --> 00:17:57.050
I told you I'm not a crybaby!

00:17:57.050 --> 00:17:58.010
What?

00:17:58.010 --> 00:18:01.970
Don't lecture me, you damn siscon!

00:18:02.930 --> 00:18:06.300
What did you say?! You're the one
who was all moody the whole time!

00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:09.600
I was imitating you!

00:18:09.600 --> 00:18:10.520
You...

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:11.650
Did you have to be so blunt?!

00:18:13.190 --> 00:18:14.150
Amazing!

00:18:14.150 --> 00:18:16.570
Those two... even while fighting...

00:18:16.570 --> 00:18:17.860
They took out that many missiles?

00:18:17.860 --> 00:18:19.530
But the time...

00:18:20.780 --> 00:18:22.740
10 seconds to Decoupling...

00:18:23.020 --> 00:18:25.750
9, 8, 7,

00:18:26.010 --> 00:18:28.620
6, 5, 4,

00:18:28.990 --> 00:18:31.500
3, 2, 1!

00:18:31.830 --> 00:18:32.960
It's time.

00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:39.630
Not yet!

00:18:43.150 --> 00:18:45.140
Coupling has been prolonged!

00:18:45.140 --> 00:18:46.390
What did you say?!

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:49.020
Impossible!

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:51.500
Secret Services Agent, your orders?

00:18:52.170 --> 00:18:54.230
C-Continue with the missile barrage!

00:18:54.540 --> 00:18:58.990
There must be some miscalculation,
but the Coupling won't last much longer!

00:18:58.990 --> 00:19:01.030
Fire, fire, fire!

00:19:05.490 --> 00:19:06.950
We'll follow them!

00:19:06.950 --> 00:19:07.700
Roger!

00:19:07.700 --> 00:19:10.920
The Coupling time has exceeded 400 seconds!

00:19:11.250 --> 00:19:12.670
I don't believe it.

00:19:20.090 --> 00:19:22.090
All missiles have been shot down!

00:19:22.090 --> 00:19:24.010
I-It can't be!

00:19:40.490 --> 00:19:42.070
E-Emergency eject!

00:19:42.780 --> 00:19:44.870
Open up! Open up!

00:19:45.460 --> 00:19:48.290
I can't die like this! Not me!

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:50.410
No!

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:55.040
Are you alright, Secret Services Agent?

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:57.880
That voice... Alfried Gallant?

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:01.510
The plan has failed. All mechas will fall back.

00:20:03.250 --> 00:20:04.510
Yes.

00:20:13.770 --> 00:20:16.690
Hey, crybaby! So you <i>can</i> do it if you try.

00:20:16.690 --> 00:20:18.280
Shut up, siscon.

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:24.780
The Coupling time for today was 429 seconds.

00:20:24.780 --> 00:20:26.280
Unbelievable.

00:20:26.740 --> 00:20:29.210
It largely exceeded the theoretical maximum.

00:20:29.210 --> 00:20:30.500
Elvira-kun.

00:20:30.500 --> 00:20:31.250
Yes?

00:20:31.550 --> 00:20:33.830
It was a nice Coupling.

00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:36.920
Professor! Professor!

00:20:37.220 --> 00:20:39.460
What's wrong? Professor!

00:20:39.460 --> 00:20:40.960
Professor!

00:21:08.990 --> 00:21:13.570
Unfortunately, the Administration Bureau has already decided to replace you.

00:21:14.210 --> 00:21:16.670
They'll get in touch with you soon.

00:21:16.670 --> 00:21:19.090
Why don't you relax until then?

00:21:19.090 --> 00:21:20.670
I envy you.

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:24.300
I haven't had a vacation in years.

00:21:24.300 --> 00:21:25.530
Doctor Hahn.

00:21:26.130 --> 00:21:28.510
What is it, Lieutenant Colonel Alfried?

00:21:28.510 --> 00:21:32.850
Direct attacks won't work while the white swan is in Hawaii.

00:21:32.850 --> 00:21:37.600
In light of that, I would like to implement
the plan in that report sent to you earlier.

00:21:37.600 --> 00:21:40.150
Report? When did you...?

00:21:40.150 --> 00:21:43.110
Your plan has been approved.

00:21:43.630 --> 00:21:46.610
You can meet up with the team any time.

00:21:46.610 --> 00:21:49.570
I'm expecting results from you, Lieutenant Colonel Alfried.

00:21:49.930 --> 00:21:51.550
Glory to Zogilia!

00:21:59.380 --> 00:22:01.710
Reinforcements at a time like this?

00:22:01.710 --> 00:22:02.960
I wonder who they are.

00:22:02.960 --> 00:22:04.050
Tarjim!

00:22:08.130 --> 00:22:11.600
I'm glad you came, Lieutenant Commander Ryazan.

00:22:12.020 --> 00:22:14.180
How are you doing, Hina?

00:22:14.180 --> 00:22:15.820
Father!

00:22:17.130 --> 00:22:20.890
With my heart, I call out

00:22:20.890 --> 00:22:25.260
To the far side, mutually drawn

00:22:25.260 --> 00:22:29.770
Forgetting even the reason I ache

00:22:29.770 --> 00:22:34.400
Just for now, please

00:22:34.400 --> 00:22:38.570
I know you

00:22:38.570 --> 00:22:43.070
I'm searching for you

00:22:43.200 --> 00:22:45.540
Softly pressing my lips

00:22:45.540 --> 00:22:52.170
to the bright afterimage I can't keep from leaving

00:22:52.170 --> 00:23:00.720
If hesitation is what gives way to the slightest of hopes

00:23:00.720 --> 00:23:05.300
To the many gentle mornings...

00:23:05.300 --> 00:23:09.850
and the times I have wondered

00:23:09.850 --> 00:23:14.110
In the future that leads back to that sky,

00:23:14.110 --> 00:23:16.360
I want to save you,

00:23:16.360 --> 00:23:18.440
I want to protect you

00:23:18.440 --> 00:23:22.820
In the future that arrives at that dream

00:23:22.820 --> 00:23:25.700
Wait for me

00:23:25.700 --> 00:23:30.460
The love we'll surely find

00:23:30.460 --> 00:23:35.250
I want you to reach out for it

00:23:38.130 --> 00:23:40.620
Next episode, on Buddy Complex:

00:23:40.620 --> 00:23:41.890
"Father and Son."
